Quiz :

1. What does def reply(text): do? Why put the mood logic inside 
   a function instead of only using print at the top of the file?

     def names a reusable block. text is the input. A function can be
     imported by tool_bot.py; top-level print cannot be reused as easily.    

2. Why text = text.lower() once?

     So every if compares lowercase. "Happy" and "happy" both match.

3. "exam" in text vs text == "exam"?

    in means the word appears anywhere. == needs an exact match. 
    I have an exam tomorrow matches in, not ==.

4. Why return instead of print?

    return sends the sentence back to the caller. 
    print(reply(feeling)) is what shows it.

5. What is if __name__ == "__main__":?

    That block runs only when you run mood_bot.py directly. 
    Importing reply from tool_bot.py skips it, 
    so the bot does not ask “How are you feeling?” twice.


